      "body_recovery_method": "wayback",
      "context_excerpt": "This upends the old economics of determining when data belongs in memory (where applications can fetch it faster) versus on a storage drive (where it can be held in cheap and plentiful space). The tradeoff was first framed 40 years ago, when the answer was measured in accessing that data in minutes. On today’s GPUs, paired with AI storage solutions from NVIDIA and partners, the same tradeoff now plays out in microseconds.",
